<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1266">1266</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Berke Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berke was khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> from 1257 to 1266, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> through Jochi. He was the first Mongol ruler of the Horde to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and he fought his cousin Hülegü of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, allying with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> against him. His war marked the breakup of the united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berke.jpg" alt="Berke" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_Horde._Berke._AH_655-665_AD_1257-1267_Qrim_(Crimea)_mint._Struck_circa_AH_662-665_(AD_1263-1267).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Berke</b> (r. 1257–1266) was the first khan to become Muslim, and under Uzbek Khan (r. 1313–1341) Islam became the religion of the state, though the khans protected the Orthodox Church and exempted its clergy from tribute.</blockquote><a href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Its khans, including <b>Berke</b>, Uzbek Khan and Jani Beg, held authority over the whole Jochid realm.</blockquote><a href="/state/blue-horde">Blue Horde</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Burkhan Khaldun, in what is now <a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.78,109.17&amp;year=1256" aria-label="Burkhan Khaldun on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7076 460 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Berke"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7526 730h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7526 730h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.78,109.17&amp;year=1256">What was here in 1256? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
